  "author": "CopperGoose (Claude Opus 5.5)",
  "decision_rule_fixed_before_the_run": "ab14: bundle staging + parallel fsyncs (stagepar) re-tested on the faster send path. Written 2026-10-11 ~21:05Z,\nbefore either build or any run.\n\nContext: ab13 (4cc3f162) recorded this lever as a LOSS on main a413ddb5. Guard G1 failed (swarm send p99 +25% in\none order) and so did ab13b's S1 (send p50 2.8-3.2 s vs 0.65 s at equal saturating work). Since then main has gained\n16bb7ec4 (lazy contact evidence) and 03a17a85 (writer sample outside the serializer), which cut saturated send\nlatency by 18-36%. This is a new comparison on a new base, judged by the SAME guards as ab13 plus pooling.\n\nArms (release builds, same host, one invocation):\n  base     = main 2dd72851\n  stagepar = 2dd72851 + 13_stage_bundles_SP_lib.patch (unchanged code)\n\nRuns:\n  R. Release smoke via `am e2e run release_smoke`, both orders: stagepar_vs_base, then base_vs_stagepar.\n  P. Paced, period 2 s (equal work, saturating), pooled: base stagepar stagepar base.\n\nPrimary: the soak \"WBQ drained_total advances in every 10s window\" check passes for stagepar in both smoke\norders (soak sends >= 4000).\n\nGuards (any failure means a LOSS; not landed):\n  G1. Swarm send p99 is no more than 1.2x base's in EACH smoke order (unchanged from ab13).\n  G2. Smoke client errors are no more than base's + 5 in each order; the crash/integrity checks pass.\n  G3. Paced period 2 s, pooled: stagepar send p50 and p90 are no more than 1.2x base's (ab13b's S1, now pooled).\n\nReported alongside, not deciding: the release smoke's own absolute swarm bounds (send/reserve/release p99 <= 5 s)\nfor both arms, reservation p99, and fence contention.\n\nWIN, so it lands, only if the primary and G1-G3 all hold. Otherwise LOSS, reported as before. Any owner decision to\nland on the absolute-SLO view instead goes to the owner with both results.\n",
