  "verdict": "LOSS under ab14_rule.txt (written before the runs); not landed.\n\nPrimary held: the stagepar soak \"WBQ drained_total advances in every 10s window\" check passed in both smoke orders (base failed it in both).\n\nGuards:\n- G1 failed in both orders. Swarm send p99 was 5.57 s vs 2.93 s (1.90x) and 4.89 s vs 3.29 s (1.49x); the guard is 1.2x.\n- G2 held: tool errors 0 and 3 vs 1 and 4; crash and soak convergence passed for both arms.\n- G3 failed. Pooled paced period 2 s send p50 was 2.40 s vs 0.48 s (5.0x), p90 3.09 vs 1.56 s (1.98x).\n\nReported, not deciding:\n- Swarm reservation p99 2.1/1.9 s vs 15.1/13.5 s.\n- Swarm sends acked 8,312/8,334 vs 6,614/6,658 (+26%).\n- Both arms failed the post-swarm archive convergence check (base 25/92 DB-only, stagepar 1,209/1,217). This is a main-wide release blocker, noted on br-kp1in.35.\n\nReading: same as ab13. Taking the fence off the reservation path lets agents saturate the serialized message insert, so send latency at saturation rises 2-5x. Send-path capacity (br-qbhs0) is the wall.\n\nHost note: the load average reached 8-14 during the paced runs from unrelated local compiles; the mirrored order (base stagepar stagepar base) spreads it over both arms."
